The input you provided is already in the structured JSON format. It contains an array of objects, each representing a vulnerability found in a function. The keys of each object are "function_name", "vulnerability", and "reason". The values for these keys are the corresponding vulnerability details.

Here is the same input in a more readable format:

```json
{
    "output_list": [
        {
            "function_name": "ValueLocked",
            "vulnerability": "Integer Overflow",
            "reason": "Integer Overflow in Sell function allows seller to lock assets."
        }
    ]
}
```

If you want to add more vulnerabilities, you can simply add more objects to the "output_list" array. For example:

```json
{
    "output_list": [
        {
            "function_name": "ValueLocked",
            "vulnerability": "Integer Overflow",
            "reason": "Integer Overflow in Sell function allows seller to lock assets."
        },
        {
            "function_name": "Withdraw",
            "vulnerability": "Unchecked Balance",
            "reason": "Unchecked balance in Withdraw function can lead to loss of assets."
        }
    ]
}
```